    <briefdescription>
<para>A vinyl statement can have either key or tuple format. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tuple statement structure: data_offset ^ +-------------------------------<mdash/>+ | 4 bytes 4 bytes MessagePack data. | +---<mdash/>+-<mdash/>+---<mdash/>+------------------------<mdash/>+- - - - - - . tuple, ..., raw: | offN | .. | off1 | header ..|key1|..|keyN|.. | operations | +<ndash/>+<mdash/>+-<mdash/>+<ndash/>+<mdash/>+------------------------<mdash/>+- - - - - - . | ... | ^ ^ | +--------------<mdash/>+ | +-----------------------------------<mdash/>+ Offsets are stored only for indexed fields, though MessagePack&apos;ed tuple data can contain also not indexed fields. For example, if fields 3 and 5 are indexed then before MessagePack data are stored offsets only for field 3 and field 5.</para><para>Key statement structure: +-----------<mdash/>+--------------<mdash/>+ | array header | part1 ... partN | - MessagePack data +-----------<mdash/>+--------------<mdash/>+</para><para>Field &apos;operations&apos; is used for storing operations of UPSERT statement. </para>    </detaileddescription>
